From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:04:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: carry the whole police action into the port policer

tc hands a matchall police action to DSA with a committed rate and burst, a
peak rate and the mtu that sizes its bucket, a packet rate and burst, an
average rate, a per-packet overhead, and what is to become of the packets that
conform and of those that do not. DSA copies two of those into
dsa_mall_policer_tc_entry and drops the rest, so a switch offered

  police rate 10mbit burst 20k peakrate 20mbit mtu 1500 conform-exceed drop/pipe

installs a single-rate meter whose exceed action is whatever its reset value
happens to be, and the user is told it worked.

Carry the fields the action already carries. Nothing changes for the two
drivers that implement .port_policer_add today: felix and sja1105 read the rate
and the burst and are unaffected by members they never touch. What changes is
that a driver can now do what every flower-side policer offload in the tree
does - validate the action and refuse with -EOPNOTSUPP the parts its meter
cannot express - which it cannot do while the core discards them first.

Only the action ids of exceed and notexceed are carried, not their extval: the
value belongs to a jump, and a port policer has no chain to jump to. Colour
awareness is likewise absent, because act_police has no field that says what
colour a packet arrived as - the mode stays unreachable on hardware that has
it, and this patch does not pretend otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/include/net/dsa.h
+++ b/include/net/dsa.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_data/dsa.h>
 #include <linux/phylink.h>
 #include <net/devlink.h>
+#include <net/flow_offload.h>
 #include <net/switchdev.h>
 
 struct dsa_8021q_context;
@@ -222,6 +223,14 @@ struct dsa_mall_mirror_tc_entry {
 struct dsa_mall_policer_tc_entry {
 	u32 burst;
 	u64 rate_bytes_per_sec;
+	u64 peakrate_bytes_per_sec;
+	u64 rate_pkt_per_sec;
+	u64 burst_pkt;
+	u32 mtu;
+	u32 avrate;
+	u16 overhead;
+	enum flow_action_id exceed_act_id;
+	enum flow_action_id notexceed_act_id;
 };
 
 /* TC matchall entry */
--- a/net/dsa/user.c
+++ b/net/dsa/user.c
@@ -1499,6 +1499,14 @@ dsa_user_add_cls_matchall_police(struct
 	policer = &mall_tc_entry->policer;
 	policer->rate_bytes_per_sec = act->police.rate_bytes_ps;
 	policer->burst = act->police.burst;
+	policer->peakrate_bytes_per_sec = act->police.peakrate_bytes_ps;
+	policer->rate_pkt_per_sec = act->police.rate_pkt_ps;
+	policer->burst_pkt = act->police.burst_pkt;
+	policer->mtu = act->police.mtu;
+	policer->avrate = act->police.avrate;
+	policer->overhead = act->police.overhead;
+	policer->exceed_act_id = act->police.exceed.act_id;
+	policer->notexceed_act_id = act->police.notexceed.act_id;
 
 	err = ds->ops->port_policer_add(ds, dp->index, policer);
 	if (err) {
